<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">The origin</p>
    <h2>A personal question became a product</h2>
    <p>After a serious health experience, founder Austin started looking more closely at hydration products: what was in them, how oral fluid absorption works and why so much of the category was built around flavour, sugar avoidance or generic electrolyte language.</p>
    <p>That became Best Hydrate: a hydration mix with a short ingredient list and a public explanation for why each ingredient is there.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">What matters</span>
    <h3>No magic ingredient. No universal use case.</h3>
    <p>The right hydration approach depends on the person, activity and setting.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">The formula</p>
    <h2>Start with ingredients that have a job</h2>
    <p>Best Hydrate combines glucose, sodium chloride, potassium chloride, sodium bicarbonate, citric acid and lemon powder. Our formula pages explain what each ingredient contributes and where the evidence is established physiology rather than a Best Hydrate-specific outcome.</p>
